# Who fixes what

Before writing code, read `docs/design/who-fixes-what.md`.

Alfred owns application logic, the database, infrastructure, and any product decision still open, and he merges those pull requests. Item 1 is draft #86. Open work awaiting him, not on that ordered list: drafts #89, #91, and #137; ready for review #134. #127 merged on 23 Oct 2026. It changed `quant/trade/order_policy.py`, `quant/trade/models/order.py`, docs, and tests. Application code. Alfred merged it. Bots do not own it. #128 closed on 25 Oct 2026, about 10:13 AM HKT, without merge. It had been ready for review. Alfred owned it while it was open. Alfred said the solution seems wrong. Bots do not own a revive or a retarget unless Alfred asks. #137 still changes `quant/trade` (`order.py`, `confirm.py`, `order_policy.py`), docs, and tests. Application code. It had followed #128. #128 is closed without merge. It stays a draft until review has passed, CI is green, and nothing is waiting on a decision. Alfred merges it. Bots do not own a revive of #128 or any retarget of #137 unless Alfred asks. Do not touch #137's branch. #134 changes a Liquibase refdata release comment and tests and is ready for review. Alfred merges it. Bots do not own it. #143 merged on 25 Oct 2026, about 10:13 AM HKT. It changed `frontend/package.json` and `frontend/package-lock.json`. Dependency files are application code, the same rule as #126. Alfred merged it. Bots do not own it. #133 merged on 25 Oct 2026, about 9:59 AM HKT. It changed `quant/api/main.py` and tests, and the API and REFDATA cache docs. Application code. Alfred merged it. Bots do not own it. #136 merged on 25 Oct 2026, about 9:57 AM HKT. It changed `quant/trade/brokers/ccxt/confirm.py` and `tests/unit/test_ccxt_confirm.py`. Application code. Alfred merged it. Bots do not own it. #138 merged on 25 Oct 2026, about 9:55 AM HKT. It changed only `tests/unit/test_order_policy.py` and `tests/unit/test_refdata_reader.py`. Test-only. Alfred merged it. Bots do not own it. #139 merged on 25 Oct 2026, about 9:55 AM HKT. It changed `scripts/appctl.sh` and `docs/architecture/dev-vs-prod.md`. Infrastructure. Alfred merged it. Bots do not own it. #126 merged on 22 Oct 2026. Alfred merged it. Bots do not own it. #129 merged on 22 Oct 2026. Alfred merged it. Bots do not own it. #124 merged on 22 Oct 2026. It changed only `scripts/bybit_local_testnet.py` and `tests/unit/test_bybit_local_testnet.py`. It is an offline harness that does not change live behaviour. Alfred merged it. #125 merged on 22 Oct 2026. It changed `quant/trade/brokers/ccxt/confirm.py` and tests. Alfred merged it. Bots do not own it. #132 merged on 22 Oct 2026. Alfred merged it. It is a docs change.

Bots own a verified small bug, docs, research notes, and an offline harness that does not change live behaviour. #135 merged on 25 Oct 2026, about 9:58 AM HKT. It changed `scripts/bybit_local_testnet.py`, `tests/unit/test_bybit_local_testnet.py`, `tests/integration/test_ccxt_dry_run.py`, and added `tests/unit/test_ccxt_dry_run_fixture.py`. Every file is on `deploy.yml` `paths-ignore`. It is an offline harness that does not change live behaviour. Alfred merged it. A test-only pull request still goes to Alfred.

A pull request stays a draft until review has passed, CI is green, and nothing is waiting on a decision. Bots never self-merge an application-code pull request (`quant/**`, frontend, Liquibase, infra). Docs must not recommend risk numbers. Every code change reuses or extends existing utilities, classes, readers, and fields. A review fails a pull request that duplicates an existing object. The rule is `docs/design/coding-standards.md`.

- If the task is on Alfred's list, do not implement it.
- If it is an open product decision, stop and say so.
- If it is on the bot list and is a verified bug under about 20 lines of real code, it can be a small fix.
- Do not push to or change the draft state of a pull request a person opened rather than a bot. Alfred reviews and merges it.
